module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FinGenFromCover.Powers
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AmpleEventualGeneration.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.SectionProduct.Stalk

/-!
# Half (2) of clause (7) of Stacks Tag 01Q3 from local generation on an ample cover

This file proves half (2) of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3],
`Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist` (every quasi-coherent module of finite
type is generated by finitely many global sections after *some* twist), for an ample invertible
`L`, from a local generation hypothesis over the affine nonvanishing opens of global sections of
the powers of `L`.

Ampleness gives a finite family of global sections `t i` of a single power `L ^⊗ N`, `N ≥ 1`,
whose nonvanishing loci are affine opens covering `X`. Over each member the hypothesis gives one
exponent `e i` and a finite family of global sections of `F ⊗ L ^⊗ (N e i)` generating it there.
Tensoring with `L ^⊗ (N (E - e i))`, which is generated by finitely many global sections, raises
every exponent to their maximum `E`, and the disjoint union of the families generates
`F ⊗ L ^⊗ (N E)` globally, by `AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates`.

The hypothesis `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist` holds for every ample
`L`, by `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isAmple`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsFinGenOn`: finitely many global sections whose germs span every
  stalk over an open.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`: over an affine nonvanishing open
  `X_s` of a global section `s` of `L ^⊗ N`, every quasi-coherent module `F` of finite type has
  `F ⊗ L ^⊗ (N e)` generated over `X_s` for one exponent `e ≥ 1`.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterTwist`: the same for every sufficiently large
  exponent.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.tensorPowShift`: `(F ⊗ L ^⊗ a) ⊗ L ^⊗ b ≅ F ⊗ L ^⊗ c` when
  `a + b = c`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGen_of_isFinGenOn_cover`: generation over each member of a
  finite open cover is generation.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGen_iff_isFinGenOn_top`: at `V = ⊤` the local predicate is
  exactly `Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen`.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenOn_of_isFinGen`,
  `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsFinGenOn.mono`: generation gives generation over every open, and
  generation over an open passes to smaller opens.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk`: generation over an open is
  surjectivity on the stalks over it of a map from a free module of finite rank, the per-point
  form of [Stacks, Tag 01AN].
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsFinGenOn.tensor`, `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsFinGenOn.of_iso`,
  `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.surjStalk_of_epi`: tensoring with an invertible module generated by
  finitely many global sections, and transport along isomorphisms and epimorphisms.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.exists_affine_nonvanishingCover`: for `L` ample, a finite cover of
  `X` by affine nonvanishing loci of global sections of one power `L ^⊗ N`.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGen_tensorPowModule_mul`: if `L ^⊗ N` is generated by
  finitely many global sections then so is `L ^⊗ (N k)` for every `k : ℕ`.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`: half (2)
  of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] from ampleness and
  `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`.
* `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterTwist`,
  `Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterTwist`: the same from
  the uniform hypothesis.

## Implementation notes

The span in `IsFinGenOn` is taken over the stalk of the `RingCat`-valued structure sheaf, the ring
`AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates` uses, acting through the scoped instance
`Stacks.FinGenFromCover.ringStalkModule`. This is not the ring `Stacks.ModuleStalk.stalkModule`
acts by, and no comparison homomorphism between the two is built.

The cover is indexed by a subtype of a `Finset` of points of `X`, which lies in `Type u`, the
universe a generating index must inhabit. The glued family is indexed by a `Sigma` type, with no
deduplication, since a repeated section only enlarges a span.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01AN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01AN)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits MonoidalCategory
open TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Ample AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules Stacks.AmpleGlobalGeneration
open scoped Stacks.ModuleStalk Stacks.FinGenFromCover

universe u

namespace Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration

attribute [local instance] Stacks.SheafOfModules.monoidalCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.symmetricCategoryPresheafOfModules
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isMonoidal_localIso
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.isLocalization_sheafify Stacks.SheafInternalHom.monoidalCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.sheafifyMonoidal Stacks.SheafInternalHom.braidedCategory
  Stacks.SheafInternalHom.schemeMonoidalCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeBraidedCategory
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemePreadditive
  Stacks.SectionRingGeometric.schemeTensorRightAdditive

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Generation by finitely many global sections over an open -/

/-- **Generation by finitely many global sections over an open subset.** An `𝒪_X`-module `M` is
generated over `V` when there are finitely many *global* sections of `M` whose germs span the
stalk of `M` at every point of `V`. -/
def IsFinGenOn (M : X.Modules) (V : X.Opens) : Prop :=
  ∃ (I : Type u) (t : I → Γ(M, ⊤)), Finite I ∧ ∀ x ∈ V,
    Submodule.span (R := (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk X.ringCatSheaf.obj x : RingCat))
      (Set.range fun i => (M.presheaf.Γgerm x).hom (t i)) = ⊤

/-- Generation over an open passes to smaller opens. -/
theorem IsFinGenOn.mono {M : X.Modules} {V W : X.Opens} (hVW : W ≤ V) (h : IsFinGenOn M V) :
    IsFinGenOn M W := by
  obtain ⟨I, t, hI, hspan⟩ := h
  exact ⟨I, t, hI, fun x hx => hspan x (hVW hx)⟩

/-- A module generated by finitely many global sections is generated over every open. -/
theorem isFinGenOn_of_isFinGen {M : X.Modules} (h : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen M)
    (V : X.Opens) : IsFinGenOn M V := by
  obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := h
  refine ⟨σ.I, fun i => (σ.s i).eval (op ⊤), hσ, fun x _ => ?_⟩
  exact (AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates X.ringCatSheaf M σ.s).mp σ.epi x

/-- Evaluating the module morphism attached to a global section at `⊤` recovers the section. -/
private theorem eval_sectionsEquiv_symm {M : X.Modules} (s : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    ((Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv X M).symm s).eval (op ⊤) = s :=
  (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv X M).apply_symm_apply s

/-- **Local generation on a finite open cover is generation.** If finitely many opens cover `X`
and `M` is generated over each of them by finitely many global sections, then `M` is generated by
finitely many global sections. -/
theorem isFinGen_of_isFinGenOn_cover {M : X.Modules} {ι : Type u} [Finite ι] (V : ι → X.Opens)
    (hcov : ∀ x : X, ∃ i, x ∈ V i) (h : ∀ i, IsFinGenOn M (V i)) :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen M := by
  choose I t hI hspan using h
  have : ∀ i, Finite (I i) := hI
  refine ⟨⟨(i : ι) × I i,
    fun p => (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv X M).symm (t p.1 p.2), ?_⟩,
    inferInstance⟩
  refine (AlgebraicGeometry.generates_iff_stalkwise_generates X.ringCatSheaf M _).mpr fun x => ?_
  simp only [eval_sectionsEquiv_symm]
  obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hcov x
  refine eq_top_iff.mpr ((hspan i x hi).ge.trans (Submodule.span_mono ?_))
  rintro - ⟨j, rfl⟩
  exact ⟨⟨i, j⟩, rfl⟩

/-- A module is generated by finitely many global sections exactly when it is generated by
finitely many global sections over `⊤`. -/
theorem isFinGen_iff_isFinGenOn_top {M : X.Modules} :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen M ↔ IsFinGenOn M ⊤ :=
  ⟨fun h => isFinGenOn_of_isFinGen h ⊤,
    fun h => isFinGen_of_isFinGenOn_cover (ι := PUnit.{u + 1}) (fun _ => ⊤)
      (fun _ => ⟨PUnit.unit, trivial⟩) fun _ => h⟩

/-! ### The bridge to stalk surjectivity, and raising a tensor factor -/

/-- An epimorphism of `𝒪_X`-modules is surjective on every stalk, in the `SurjStalk` spelling. -/
theorem surjStalk_of_epi {M N : X.Modules} (f : M ⟶ N) (hf : Epi f) (x : X) :
    Stacks.SectionProduct.SurjStalk f x := by
  have hf' : Epi (C := SheafOfModules.{u} X.ringCatSheaf) f := hf
  exact (AlgebraicGeometry.epi_iff_stalk_surjective X.ringCatSheaf f).mp hf' x

/-- **Generation over an open, as surjectivity of a stalk map.** `IsFinGenOn M V` holds exactly
when some morphism from a free module on a finite index type is surjective on the stalk at every
point of `V`. -/
theorem isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk {M : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens} :
    IsFinGenOn M V ↔ ∃ (I : Type u) (_ : Finite I) (φ : freeModule X I ⟶ M),
      ∀ x ∈ V, Stacks.SectionProduct.SurjStalk φ x := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨I, t, hI, hspan⟩
    refine ⟨I, hI, M.freeHomEquiv.symm
      (fun i => (Stacks.NonvanishingSpelling.sectionsEquiv X M).symm (t i)), fun x hx => ?_⟩
    refine (AlgebraicGeometry.freeHom_stalk_surjective_iff_span X.ringCatSheaf M _ x).mpr ?_
    simp only [eval_sectionsEquiv_symm]
    exact hspan x hx
  · rintro ⟨I, hI, φ, hφ⟩
    refine ⟨I, fun i => (M.freeHomEquiv φ i).eval (op ⊤), hI, fun x hx => ?_⟩
    refine (AlgebraicGeometry.freeHom_stalk_surjective_iff_span X.ringCatSheaf M
      (M.freeHomEquiv φ) x).mp ?_
    exact Eq.mpr (congrArg (fun f => Stacks.SectionProduct.SurjStalk f x)
      (M.freeHomEquiv.symm_apply_apply φ)) (hφ x hx)

/-- Generation over an open transports along an isomorphism. -/
theorem IsFinGenOn.of_iso {M N : X.Modules} {V : X.Opens} (h : IsFinGenOn M V) (e : M ≅ N) :
    IsFinGenOn N V := by
  obtain ⟨I, hI, φ, hφ⟩ := isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk.mp h
  exact isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk.mpr ⟨I, hI, φ ≫ e.hom, fun x hx =>
    (hφ x hx).comp (Stacks.SectionProduct.surjStalk_of_inv e.inv_hom_id x)⟩

/-- **Raising a tensor factor.** If `M` is generated over `V` by finitely many global sections and
an invertible `P` is generated by finitely many global sections, then `M ⊗ P` is generated over
`V` by finitely many global sections. -/
theorem IsFinGenOn.tensor {M P : X.Modules} [IsInvertibleModule X P] {V : X.Opens}
    (hM : IsFinGenOn M V) (hP : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen P) :
    IsFinGenOn (M ⊗ P) V := by
  obtain ⟨I, hI, φ, hφ⟩ := isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk.mp hM
  obtain ⟨τ, hτ⟩ := hP
  have := hI
  have := hτ
  refine isFinGenOn_iff_exists_surjStalk.mpr ⟨I × τ.I, inferInstance,
    (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.freeProdIso I τ.I).hom ≫
      Limits.Sigma.map (fun _ : I => (τ.π : freeModule X τ.I ⟶ P)) ≫
      (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.freeTensorIso I P).inv ≫ (φ ▷ P), fun x hx => ?_⟩
  refine (Stacks.SectionProduct.surjStalk_of_inv
      (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.freeProdIso I τ.I).inv_hom_id x).comp
    ((surjStalk_of_epi _
        (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.epi_sigma_map _ fun _ => τ.epi) x).comp
      ((Stacks.SectionProduct.surjStalk_of_inv
          (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.freeTensorIso I P).hom_inv_id x).comp
        (Stacks.SectionProduct.SurjStalk.whiskerRight φ P (hφ x hx))))

/-! ### The ample cover in one degree -/

variable (L : X.Modules) [IsInvertibleModule X L]

/-- **The affine cover that ampleness provides, in a single degree.** For `L` ample there is one
degree `N ≥ 1` and a finite family of global sections `t i` of `L ^⊗ N` whose nonvanishing loci
are affine opens covering `X`. -/
theorem exists_affine_nonvanishingCover (hL : IsAmple X L) :
    ∃ (N : ℕ) (S : Finset X) (t : {y : X // y ∈ S} → Γ(tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ), ⊤))
      (U : {y : X // y ∈ S} → X.Opens), 1 ≤ N ∧
      (∀ i, (U i : Set X) = nonvanishingLocus (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ)) (t i)) ∧
        (∀ i, IsAffineOpen (U i)) ∧ ∀ x : X, ∃ i, x ∈ U i := by
  have := hL.compactSpace
  have hpt : ∀ x : X, ∃ (n : ℕ) (a : Stacks.GradedSections.powSections L n) (W : X.Opens),
      1 ≤ n ∧ (W : Set X) = Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.nvLocus L a ∧ x ∈ W ∧
        IsAffineOpen W := by
    intro x
    obtain ⟨n, hn, s, W, hW, hxW, hWaff⟩ :=
      IsAmpleForPowers.exists_affine_nonvanishingLocus (pow := tensorPowModule X L) hL x
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.exists_powSections_nvLocus_eq L n s
    exact ⟨n, a, W, hn, by rw [hW, ha], hxW, hWaff⟩
  choose n a W hn hWeq hxW hWaff using hpt
  obtain ⟨S, hS⟩ := isCompact_univ.elim_finite_subcover
    (fun y : X => Stacks.AmpleFiniteAvoidance.nvLocus L (a y))
    (fun y => Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isOpen_nvLocus L (a y))
    fun x _ => Set.mem_iUnion.mpr ⟨x, by rw [← hWeq x]; exact hxW x⟩
  obtain ⟨N, b, hN, hb⟩ := Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_common_degree_family L
    (ι := {y : X // y ∈ S}) (fun i => n i.1) (fun i => hn i.1) fun i => a i.1
  choose t ht using fun i : {y : X // y ∈ S} =>
    Stacks.FinGenFromCover.exists_global_nonvanishingLocus_eq L N (b i)
  refine ⟨N, S, t, fun i => W i.1, hN, fun i => ?_, fun i => hWaff i.1, fun x => ?_⟩
  · rw [hWeq i.1, ← hb i, ← ht i]
  · obtain ⟨y, hy, hxy⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion₂.mp (hS (Set.mem_univ x))
    exact ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, show x ∈ (W y : Set X) by rw [hWeq y]; exact hxy⟩

/-! ### Multiples of a generated degree -/

/-- **Every nonnegative multiple of a generated degree is generated.** If `L ^⊗ N` is generated by
finitely many global sections then so is `L ^⊗ (N k)` for every `k : ℕ`. -/
theorem isFinGen_tensorPowModule_mul {N : ℕ}
    (h : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ))) (k : ℕ) :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X L ((N * k : ℕ) : ℤ)) := by
  induction k with
  | zero => simpa using Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.isFinGen_tensorPowModule_zero (L := L)
  | succ m ih =>
    refine Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen.tensorPow_add ?_ ih h
    push_cast
    ring

/-- Shifting the twist on a module: `(F ⊗ L ^⊗ a) ⊗ L ^⊗ b ≅ F ⊗ L ^⊗ c` when `a + b = c`. -/
def tensorPowShift (F : X.Modules) {a b c : ℤ} (h : a + b = c) :
    (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L a) ⊗ tensorPowModule X L b ≅ F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L c :=
  α_ F _ _ ≪≫ whiskerLeftIso F (Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.tensorPowAdd h)

/-! ### Half (2) from ampleness and local generation after twisting -/

variable (X)

/-- **Local generation after one twist**, the hypothesis for half (2) of clause (7) of
[Stacks, Tag 01Q3]: for every quasi-coherent module `F` of finite type, every `N ≥ 1` and every
global section `s` of `L ^⊗ N` whose nonvanishing locus `V` is affine, there is an exponent `e ≥ 1`
such that `F ⊗ L ^⊗ (N e)` is generated over `V` by finitely many global sections. -/
def IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist : Prop :=
  ∀ F : X.Modules, F.IsQuasicoherent → SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F →
    ∀ N : ℕ, 1 ≤ N → ∀ s : Γ(tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ), ⊤), ∀ V : X.Opens,
      (V : Set X) = nonvanishingLocus (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ)) s → IsAffineOpen V →
        ∃ e : ℕ, 1 ≤ e ∧ IsFinGenOn (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L ((N * e : ℕ) : ℤ)) V

/-- **Half (2) of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] for an ample `L`**, from
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist`: every quasi-coherent module of finite
type is generated by finitely many global sections after some twist by a power of `L`. -/
theorem isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (h : IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L) :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L := by
  intro F hFqc hFft
  obtain ⟨N, S, t, U, hN, hUeq, hUaff, hUcov⟩ := exists_affine_nonvanishingCover L hL
  have hcovL : ∀ x : X, ∃ i, x ∈ nonvanishingLocus (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ)) (t i) :=
    fun x => (hUcov x).imp fun i hi => by rwa [← hUeq i]
  have hLN : Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGen (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ)) :=
    Stacks.FinGenFromCover.isFinGen_of_nonvanishingCover _ t hcovL
  choose e he hgen using fun i : {y : X // y ∈ S} =>
    h F hFqc hFft N hN (t i) (U i) (hUeq i) (hUaff i)
  obtain ⟨E, hE⟩ := Finite.exists_le e
  refine ⟨((N * E : ℕ) : ℤ), isFinGen_of_isFinGenOn_cover U hUcov fun i => ?_⟩
  have harith : ((N * e i : ℕ) : ℤ) + ((N * (E - e i) : ℕ) : ℤ) = ((N * E : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
    rw [← Nat.cast_add, ← Nat.mul_add, Nat.add_sub_of_le (hE i)]
  exact ((hgen i).tensor (isFinGen_tensorPowModule_mul L hLN (E - e i))).of_iso
    (tensorPowShift L F harith)

/-- **Local generation after every large twist**: for every quasi-coherent module `F` of finite
type, every `N ≥ 1` and every global section `s` of `L ^⊗ N` whose nonvanishing locus `V` is
affine, there is `e₀ ≥ 1` such that `F ⊗ L ^⊗ (N e)` is generated over `V` by finitely many global
sections for every `e ≥ e₀`. -/
def IsLocallyFinGenAfterTwist : Prop :=
  ∀ F : X.Modules, F.IsQuasicoherent → SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.{u, u, u} F →
    ∀ N : ℕ, 1 ≤ N → ∀ s : Γ(tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ), ⊤), ∀ V : X.Opens,
      (V : Set X) = nonvanishingLocus (tensorPowModule X L (N : ℤ)) s → IsAffineOpen V →
        ∃ e₀ : ℕ, 1 ≤ e₀ ∧ ∀ e : ℕ, e₀ ≤ e →
          IsFinGenOn (F ⊗ tensorPowModule X L ((N * e : ℕ) : ℤ)) V

/-- Local generation after every large twist implies local generation after one twist. -/
theorem isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterTwist
    (h : IsLocallyFinGenAfterTwist X L) : IsLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L := by
  intro F hq hf N hN s V hV hVaff
  obtain ⟨e₀, he₀, hgen⟩ := h F hq hf N hN s V hV hVaff
  exact ⟨e₀, he₀, hgen e₀ le_rfl⟩

/-- **Half (2) of clause (7) of [Stacks, Tag 01Q3] for an ample `L`**, from
`Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration.IsLocallyFinGenAfterTwist`: every quasi-coherent module of finite
type is generated by finitely many global sections after some twist by a power of `L`. -/
theorem isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterTwist (hL : IsAmple X L)
    (h : IsLocallyFinGenAfterTwist X L) :
    Stacks.AmpleEventualGeneration.IsFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L :=
  isFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist X L hL
    (isLocallyFinGenAfterSomeTwist_of_isLocallyFinGenAfterTwist X L h)

end Stacks.AmpleLocalGeneration

end
